Supplementary Code S2
Protein–Ligand Interaction Analysis, Ligand Burial, Interaction Fingerprinting, and Ligand Efficiency Calculations

Purpose
This script performs post-docking structural analyses for the top-ranked KEAP1–ligand complexes.

The following analyses are performed:

1. Ligand burial using solvent accessible surface area (SASA)
2. Protein–ligand interaction fingerprinting
3. Ligand efficiency calculation
4. Export of all calculated descriptors

Input
Protein–ligand complex PDB files

Output
Supplementary_Complete_Analysis.csv

Software
Python 3.11
Biopython >=1.85
RDKit >=2024
Pandas >=2.2

Author
Umair Wahedi et al.

Notes
The Shrake–Rupley algorithm implemented in Bio.PDB is used for SASA
calculation.

Burial percentage is calculated as

%Burial =
((Estimated SASAunbound − SASAbound) /
 Estimated SASAunbound) × 100

Estimated unbound SASA is approximated as
15 Å² × number of ligand atoms.

This script is intended for comparative analysis of docked complexes and
should not be interpreted as an absolute measure of solvent exposure.
